nd": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376570, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QHYMwJ4FTBYnECVeY5HcWz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 380155, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own comment says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. The test file is unchanged.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognise that ID. The fix is based only on the test and the code comment.\n\nThe PR isn't merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014sW8q4fMRpKuGbsiu3zV7X", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NMjctJiq5ZHs1MqeKkZ1Xw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017yhmxwQaMS6DCKM97tTHct", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Y7XYQnRvtJZwouWp9bT81e", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01U28L1gp3LsSove4tf4iuwo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KXefwyFNmVY7mHu2SgsNX9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-round-half-even", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-round-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016EaJyz6UtXwhb4r25mo4Zc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QHYMwJ4FTBYnECVeY5HcWz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-round-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own comment says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. The test file is unchanged.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognise that ID. The fix is based only on the test and the code comment.\n\nThe PR isn't merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}